        "notes": "Serpico contains themes and visuals intended for mature audiences. The game includes the following content:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Fantasy violence: Players engage in frequent combat using melee weapons. Blood is depicted during combat, and some enemies may be dismembered or exhibit grotesque or corrupted forms.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Dark themes: The story explores death, grief, loss, and moral ambiguity. Some characters may experience hallucinations, religious trauma, or spiritual corruption.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Mild alcohol use: Some NPCs reference or are depicted drinking in casual or ceremonial settings.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Horror elements: Certain environments and creatures are designed to evoke fear, including unsettling imagery, disturbing sounds, and references to possession or madness.\r\n\r\nThe game does not include depictions of sexual acts, sexual assault, or non-consensual sex. There are no scenes of self-harm or suicide. However, players sensitive to intense themes of psychological distress, cult-like fanaticism, or existential horror should proceed with discretion."
